{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba openspec/changes/lint-audit-skill/mission/validations/smoke-test-200.md | sed -n '1,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Smoke Test: 200-iteration edge case loop\n     2\t\n     3\t## Result: PASS (197/200 real tests, 3 bugs found and fixed)\n     4\t\n     5\t## Summary\n     6\t\n     7\tRan 200 unique test scenarios against `skills/lint-audit/audit.sh`. Each test created a temporary project directory with specific package.json, tsconfig.json, and optional oxlint config, ran audit.sh, and verified the JSON output.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Bugs Found and Fixed\n    10\t\n    11\t1. **Test 39: malformed tsconfig compilerOptions** -- `compilerOptions` set to a string instead of object crashed jq. Fixed with type check guard.\n    12\t2. **Test 63: tsconfig root is array** -- `tsconfig.json` containing `[]` instead of `{}` crashed jq. Same fix extended to check root type.\n    13\t3. **Test 188: rules field is array** -- `.oxlintrc.json` with `\"rules\": []` instead of `{}` crashed jq. Fixed with type check before indexing.\n    14\t\n    15\tAll 3 fixes committed in `d66eb18`.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Test Categories Covered\n    18\t\n    19\t| Category | Tests | Result |\n    20\t|----------|-------|--------|\n    21\t| Linter detection (oxlint, eslint, both, neither) | 1-10 | 10/10 |\n    22\t| Type-aware detection | 11-15 | 5/5 |\n    23\t| Oxlint config formats (.json, .jsonc, .ts, multiple) | 16-20 | 5/5 |\n    24\t| Rule comparison (enabled, missing, disabled, warn) | 21-26 | 6/6 |\n    25\t| tsconfig detection (strict, missing, variants) | 27-30 | 4/4 |\n    26\t| Monorepo tsconfig scenarios | 31-35 | 5/5 |\n    27\t| Config edge cases (malformed, empty, .ts only) | 36-40 | 4/5 (1 fix) |\n    28\t| Rule status edge cases (mixed, unknown, array config) | 41-50 | 10/10 |\n    29\t| Package.json variations (scoped, plugins, workspace) | 51-60 | 10/10 |\n    30\t| tsconfig variations (false, null, string, array) | 61-70 | 9/10 (1 fix) |\n    31\t| JSONC and config.ts variants | 71-77 | 7/7 |\n    32\t| Monorepo combos (mixed strict, turborepo) | 78-80 | 3/3 |\n    33\t| Stress tests (100% config, 100 unknown rules, 20 subprojects) | 81-100 | 20/20 |\n    34\t| Per-rule enabled/disabled verification | 101-130 | 30/30 |\n    35\t| Monorepo + config combos | 131-150 | 20/20 |\n    36\t| Output schema validation | 151-170 | 20/20 |\n    37\t| Schema field presence checks | 171-180 | 10/10 (test harness escaping issue, not a real bug) |\n    38\t| Adversarial inputs (duplicate rules, null rules, array rules) | 181-200 | 19/20 (1 fix) |\n    39\t\n    40\t## Test Harness Notes\n    41\t\n    42\t- Tests 171-180 initially showed failures due to jq escaping in the test harness `eval`, not actual schema issues. Verified manually that all findings have the required fields.\n    43\t- Test 99 (unreadable directory) is environment-dependent and was excluded from the count.\n    44\t- All fixes were regression-tested against the worker's original test suite (`audit-sh.sh`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
