{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"lint-audit|skills/\" install.sh README.md ARCH.md'","aggregated_output":"rg: failed to read the file specified in RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH: /Users/stuart/.ripgreprc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nARCH.md:9:**Orchestrator** -- the main Claude Code session. Plans the work, dispatches one worker at a time, runs validators, manages fix loops and circuit breakers. Uses plan mode to keep instructions alive across long conversations. Defined by `skills/mission/SKILL.md` (10 phases, 0-9). In basic mode (`--basic`), the orchestrator also acts as the builder -- no workers are dispatched. Defined by `skills/mission/basic/SKILL.md`.\nARCH.md:45:Skills live in `skills/` at the repo root. `install.sh` symlinks each into `~/.claude/skills/` for Claude Code discovery.\nARCH.md:53:24 skills total: mission (with basic sub-skill), mission-resume, mission-status, mission-init, grill, language, prd, tdd, test-quality, security, adversarial, dispatch, artifact-review, lint-audit, skill-review, arch-review, domain-model, module-design, qa, write-a-skill, frontend, ui-system, react-perf.\nARCH.md:55:lint-audit audits a TypeScript project's oxlint config and tsconfig strictness against an agent-friendly ruleset. Part of the mechanical enforcement stack alongside the ts-quality.sh PostToolUse hook: the hook catches patterns at edit time (grep-based), the linter catches them at build time (AST-level via oxlint), and the compiler catches them at type-check time (tsconfig strictness). Gate 4 of the scrutiny validator runs the project's linter, so rules added by lint-audit are automatically enforced during missions.\nARCH.md:71:Defined by `skills/mission/basic/SKILL.md`. The main `skills/mission/SKILL.md` routes to it when `--basic` is present in the arguments.\nREADME.md:197:| `/lint-audit` | Audit a TypeScript project's oxlint config and tsconfig strictness against an agent-friendly ruleset. Reports gaps and offers to apply fixes per-item or all-at-once. Oxlint only -- skips ESLint projects. Standalone. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
